WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:05.823
How does one fertilized egg become a body?

2
00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:11.023
Gastrulation organizes the embryo into layers that make different tissues.

3
00:00:12.223 --> 00:00:15.703
Cells move from the surface to the inside and sort into germ layers.

4
00:00:16.723 --> 00:00:21.563
Most animals form three: ectoderm outside, mesoderm in the middle, and endoderm

5
00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:26.263
inside. In vertebrates, ectoderm makes epidermis and nervous tissue.

6
00:00:27.203 --> 00:00:28.743
Mesoderm makes muscle and blood.

7
00:00:29.743 --> 00:00:31.683
Endoderm makes the gut and airway lining.

8
00:00:31.683 --> 00:00:36.063
Arranging the cells sets up where different body tissues will develop.

9
00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:38.303
The movements differ.

10
00:00:39.223 --> 00:00:41.443
In invagination, a sheet bends inward.

11
00:00:42.343 --> 00:00:45.343
In involution, it rolls over an edge and spreads inside.

12
00:00:46.263 --> 00:00:49.203
In ingression, single cells leave a sheet and move inward.

13
00:00:50.323 --> 00:00:52.463
Germ layers make tissues, not whole organs.

14
00:00:53.403 --> 00:00:58.363
An intestine has endoderm lining, with mesoderm muscle and connective tissue around

15
00:00:58.363 --> 00:01:02.003
it. Neural crest cells from ectoderm add nerve cells.

16
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:04.653
What tells a cell what to become?

17
00:01:05.513 --> 00:01:07.753
Both what it inherits and signals it receives.

18
00:01:08.813 --> 00:01:13.673
Cytoplasmic determinants are molecules placed in regions of the egg and inherited by

19
00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:19.033
cells there. Induction is a signal from one group of cells that changes the fate of

20
00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:24.913
neighbours. The amphibian organizer shows this: a graft recruited host cells into a

21
00:01:24.913 --> 00:01:30.773
second body axis. Most embryos studied closely use both inherited factors and

22
00:01:30.773 --> 00:01:31.773
induction.

23
00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:34.447
Earlier, cleavage supplies the cells.

24
00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:39.447
After fertilization, the egg divides into smaller cells without growing.

25
00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:41.507
Each is a blastomere.

26
00:01:42.427 --> 00:01:44.307
Yolk slows or blocks the cleavage furrow.

27
00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:48.607
In birds, only a disc of cytoplasm on top of the yolk divides.

28
00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.610
Fertilization starts the process.

29
00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:54.430
Sperm and egg fuse to form a zygote.

30
00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:58.790
A calcium wave activates the egg and restarts the cell cycle.

31
00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.210
Eggs also block extra sperm.

32
00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:05.450
In mice, reviews conclude the membrane block is not electrical.

33
00:02:06.533 --> 00:02:08.253
Now follow one tissue forward.

34
00:02:09.173 --> 00:02:14.253
In frogs, birds and mammals, the neural plate folds into a hollow neural tube, the

35
00:02:14.253 --> 00:02:15.933
future brain and spinal cord.

36
00:02:17.093 --> 00:02:21.333
Neural crest forms at the plate edges and makes peripheral neurons and much of the

37
00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:22.833
skeleton of the face and skull.
